{
  "id": "#007",
  "title": "Silicon Micro-Nozzles: Bosch-Process DRIE in Industrial Piezo Printheads",
  "subtitle": "How deep reactive-ion etching overcomes fluid cavitation and acoustic crosstalk at 50 kHz droplet firing rates.",
  "subject": "Fluids",
  "date": "2026-10-25",
  "tangents": {
    "acoustic_impedance": {
      "tag": "WAVE DYNAMICS // ACOUSTIC CAVITIES",
      "title": "Acoustic Impedance & Reflection Coefficients",
      "body": "<p>Acoustic impedance ($Z = \\rho \\cdot c$) dictates how acoustic pressure waves transmit or reflect across fluid-solid boundaries. In silicon micro-channels, the impedance mismatch between silicon ($Z_{\\text{Si}} \\approx 19.7 \\times 10^6 \\text{Pa}\\cdot\\text{s/m}$) and ink ($Z_{\\text{fluid}} \\approx 1.5 \\times 10^6 \\text{Pa}\\cdot\\text{s/m}$) creates a reflection coefficient $R > 0.85$, reflecting acoustic pressure pulses back into the nozzle orifice to propel micro-droplets.</p>",
      "equation": "Z = \\rho \\cdot c, \\quad R = \\frac{Z_{\\text{Si}} - Z_{\\text{ink}}}{Z_{\\text{Si}} + Z_{\\text{ink}}}"
    },
    "helmholtz_resonance": {
      "tag": "FLUID DYNAMICS // CAVITY OSCILLATION",
      "title": "Helmholtz Resonance & Meniscus Frequency Limits",
      "body": "<p>The natural acoustic frequency of a fluid-filled cavity bounds the maximum firing rate before droplet volume destabilizes. Operating printheads above this resonance frequency causes acoustic wave superposition, leading to severe volume variation and droplet misdirection.</p>",
      "equation": "f_H = \\frac{c}{2\\pi} \\sqrt{\\frac{A}{V \\cdot L_{\\text{eff}}}}"
    },
    "bosch_drie": {
      "tag": "MICROFABRICATION // PLASMA PROCESSING",
      "title": "The Bosch Deep Reactive-Ion Etching Cycle",
      "body": "<p>A cyclic plasma etching process that alternates between SF6 chemical etching and C4F8 fluorocarbon passivation to achieve ultra-deep, vertical sidewalls in single-crystal silicon without lateral undercut.</p>",
      "equation": "SF_6 + e^- \\to S_x F_y^+ + F^*, \\quad n(C_4F_8) \\to (CF_2)_n"
    },
    "ohnesorge_number": {
      "tag": "DIMENSIONLESS PHYSICS // DROPLET JETTING",
      "title": "Ohnesorge Number & Jetting Stability Window",
      "body": "<p>The Ohnesorge number quantifies the relative importance of viscous forces versus inertial and surface tension forces. For stable drop-on-demand ejection without satellite droplet generation or excessive viscous damping, the fluid must satisfy $0.1 < Oh < 1.0$.</p>",
      "equation": "Oh = \\frac{\\mu}{\\sqrt{\\rho \\cdot \\sigma \\cdot d}}"
    },
    "rayleigh_plateau": {
      "tag": "HYDRODYNAMICS // CAPILLARY PINCH-OFF",
      "title": "Rayleigh-Plateau Capillary Instability",
      "body": "<p>Driven by surface tension minimization, a cylindrical column of liquid is inherently unstable to axisymmetrical surface perturbations with wavelengths exceeding the liquid circumference ($\\lambda > \\pi d$), triggering pinch-off into discrete spherical droplets.</p>",
      "equation": "\\lambda_{\\text{opt}} = \\sqrt{2} \\pi d \\approx 4.51 \\cdot d"
    },
    "pzt_transverse_strain": {
      "tag": "SMART MATERIALS // FERROELECTRIC TRANSDUCTION",
      "title": "Lead Zirconate Titanate (PZT) Transverse Actuation",
      "body": "<p>When an electric field $E_z$ is applied across the thickness of a polarized $(100)$-textured perovskite PZT thin film, it induces in-plane compressive strain through the $d_{31}$ piezoelectric coefficient, flexing the silicon diaphragm downward into the fluid cavity.</p>",
      "equation": "\\epsilon_x = \\epsilon_y = d_{31} \\cdot E_z = d_{31} \\cdot \\frac{V}{t_{\\text{PZT}}}"
    }
  },
